  "text": "Recipe: Sweet Potato Tikki with Green Chutney\nCreator: Frank Lee\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: 3 medium sweet potatoes, 1 finely chopped green chili, 1 tsp ginger-garlic paste, 1/4 tsp turmeric, 1/2 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp cumin powder, 1/2 tsp amchoor (mango powder), 1/2 tsp chaat masala, 1/2 tsp salt, 2 Tbsp mint chopped, 2 Tbsp coriander chopped, 2 Tbsp corn flour, 1 cup coriander, 1/2 cup mint, 3 cloves garlic, 3 inch ginger, 3 green chillies, 2 Tbsp roasted chana dal, 1/2 tsp cumin powder, 1 tsp chaat masala (optional), 1/4 tsp salt, a pinch of asafetida ('heeng'), 1/2 cup water, 1/2 lemon\nCooking methods: steam, roast, blend\nInstructions: TIKKI: Make a dough from 3 medium sweet potatoes – steamed & grated, 1 finely chopped green chili, 1 tsp ginger-garlic paste, 1/4 tsp turmeric, 1/2 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp cumin powder, 1/2 tsp amchoor (mango powder), 1/2 tsp chaat masala, 1/2 tsp salt, 2 Tbsp mint chopped, 2 Tbsp coriander chopped, 2 Tbsp corn flour. Make small-sized 'tikkis' using the dough. Roast them on a non-stick pan or oven. GREEN CHUTNEY: Blend this mixture into a smooth chutney: 1 cup coriander, 1/2 cup mint, 3 cloves garlic, 3 inch ginger, 3 green chillies, 2 Tbsp roasted chana dal, 1/2 tsp cumin powder, 1 tsp chaat masala, (optional) 1/4 tsp salt, a pinch of asafetida ('heeng'), 1/2 cup water. Squeeze 1/2 lemon and stir.\nNotes: Sub-recipes: TIKKI, GREEN CHUTNEY. A recipe with TUBERS (potatoes), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (lemon), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
